9b1a6edd-8ee9-4742-a79c-781f1b3b2ece	28414dac-ea5d-4ff4-9d15-fb9c96e76b97	Based on the teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, the breath is a profound link between the body and mind, offering a powerful pathway to transform consciousness and emotional states.\n\nThe breath serves as a remarkable bridge that can help you navigate your inner landscape. When you're experiencing turbulent emotions like anger or anxiety, you can use your breath as a tool for transformation. There are two interconnected approaches:\n\n1. Observing the Mind through Breath:\nYou can calm your mind by consciously observing your breath. As you become aware of your breathing, your thoughts begin to settle, creating a space of inner stillness.\n\n2. Using Breath to Soothe the Mind:\nConversely, by intentionally regulating your breath, you can directly influence your mental and emotional state. When anger or negative emotions arise, conscious breathing can help restore inner balance.\n\nSri Krishnaji emphasizes that the goal is not to control thoughts rigidly, but to cultivate a state of consciousness that minimizes negative emotions. The breath becomes a gentle guide in this journey of inner transformation.\n\nThe ultimate aim is to develop a consciousness that allows you to:\n- Move beyond possessiveness\n- Release hurt and anger\n- Cultivate love and understanding\n\nBy practicing awareness and using breath as a tool, you can aspire to become an extraordinary human being, capable of navigating life's complexities with grace and love.\n\nWatch more here: \n- \n- \n\nNamaste.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Pfat_DztMI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-18 06:48:02+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tier": "fast", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/wa