3351c1da-aabe-48ba-a1de-c327510c0b7f	7fabf934-c0cf-4f72-93ff-65e037e85c84	Based on the available context, I can share insights about karma from Sri Krishnaji's teachings:\n\nKarma is a universal law of cause and effect. Sri Krishnaji explains this principle simply: every cause generates an effect. Just as in a physical example where pushing a glass causes water to fall, karma operates similarly in our lives - our actions (causes) create corresponding consequences (effects).\n\nThis universal law suggests that our choices, thoughts, and actions are not random, but interconnected. Each action we take generates a corresponding result, creating a continuous cycle of cause and effect in our spiritual and material existence.\n\nWhile the context provides a basic understanding, I recommend exploring more deeply through their teachings to gain a comprehensive perspective on karma.\n\nWatch more here: \n- \n- \n\nMay you reflect on the profound interconnectedness of your actions and their consequences with compassion and wisdom.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7b6tnI7VmB4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EqnSkAzfIg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ji-hdW1t30g", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V45jIC4RthQ"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-18 18:25:33+00	{}	default
5757c52b-5a53-4a02-add3-98dbe6179130	c5f48307-832a-4d09-a677-44e230aea04d	Based on the teachings retrieved, here's a compassionate guidance on handling anxiety:\n\nAnxiety is not something to fight against, but a signal to understand and transform. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji's teachings suggest that anxiety itself is the primary obstacle preventing you from solving your challenges. When you are consumed by stress, your inner turbulence blocks clear perception and effective problem-solving.\n\nThe key is to consciously shift your focus from external circumstances to your internal state. Instead of being overwhelmed, you have two fundamental choices:\n\n1. Give into anxiety\n2. Choose a different path of inner transformation\n\nThe path of transformation involves:\n- Recognizing that you have very little control over external events\n- Accepting the reality of life's unpredictability\n- Focusing on your response rather than trying to control outcomes\n- Deliberately dissolving the stress clouding your perception\n\nThis isn't about suppressing anxiety, but consciously transcending it. By turning inward and choosing peace, you create space for clarity and genuine solutions to emerge.\n\nA practical approach is to:\n- Acknowledge your anxiety without judgment\n- Take deep breaths\n- Remind yourself that this moment is temporary\n- Shift your focus to what you can influence\n\nRemember, peace is not the absence of challenges, but the presence of inner calm amidst them.\n\nWatch more here: \n- \n-	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6rLvPzNyLRw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWXe9v7PHDs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6X1TVEFHAY"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-18 18:25:33+00	{}	default
