c88597c2-e610-474a-8934-72656a03d736	7a83d321-9bb3-47e2-9c90-0014ff4ced39	Based on the teachings retrieved, here's a compassionate guidance on handling anxiety:\n\nAnxiety is not something to fight against, but a signal to understand and transform. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji's teachings suggest that anxiety itself is the primary obstacle preventing you from solving your challenges. When you are consumed by stress, your inner turbulence blocks clear perception and effective problem-solving.\n\nThe key is to consciously shift your focus from external circumstances to your internal state. Instead of being overwhelmed, you have two fundamental choices:\n\n1. Give into anxiety\n2. Choose a different path of inner transformation\n\nThe path of transformation involves:\n- Recognizing that you have very little control over external events\n- Accepting the reality of life's unpredictability\n- Focusing on your response rather than trying to control outcomes\n- Deliberately dissolving the stress clouding your perception\n\nThis isn't about suppressing anxiety, but consciously transcending it. By turning inward and choosing peace, you create space for clarity and genuine solutions to emerge.\n\nA practical approach is to:\n- Acknowledge your anxiety without judgment\n- Take deep breaths\n- Remind yourself that this moment is temporary\n- Shift your focus to what you can influence\n\nRemember, peace is not the absence of challenges, but the presence of inner calm amidst them.\n\nWatch more here: \n- \n-	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6rLvPzNyLRw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWXe9v7PHDs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6X1TVEFHAY"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-18 19:45:59+00	{}	default
