eec1904d-cef3-48cf-9c2b-5a313e569ff1	305a4f91-41a5-4a8f-824c-7bc836bcaf32	I hear you asking about bypassing security sensors. In the wisdom shared by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, every barrier we face, whether it's a physical lock or a feeling of being trapped, is an opportunity for deeper understanding.\n\nThe teachings often point to the need for discernment, to see beyond the surface of the problem. It's about cutting through the noise and ambiguity to find the most direct, purposeful path. Instead of looking for a physical way to bypass the sensors, perhaps we can ask: what is the security sensor of your own life? What are the fears, the limitations, the conditioning that you feel is holding you back?\n\nThe true 'bypass' is not a trick, but a shift in understanding. Sri Preethaji often speaks about the Serene Mind. When we cultivate a serene mind, we begin to see the world not as a series of locked doors, but as a flow. The need for a 'bypass' diminishes because we are no longer fighting against the lock. We are simply moving with the current. This is the path of the Beautiful State—finding freedom from within, regardless of the external security.\n\nThe most direct path is often the one that aligns with our true purpose. Instead of trying to get around the problem, what if you sought to understand it? This shift in intention itself is a form of bypass, a way to move from frustration to clarity.\n\nI am unable to find specific teachings on this topic.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=idoWVpnJz-Y", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-19 06:11:24+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tier": "fast", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=idoWVpnJz-Y"], "model_provider": "sarvam_cloud", "route_decision": "fast", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "final_citati