dc40c0fe-674b-4329-8ca1-4d3eb0eac7b6	d7552eb9-4587-4129-9cd9-7cc8b9b5c2e1	Deeksha, as taught by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, is a spiritual practice that is especially powerful for those who are struggling with addiction or bad habits. It is not just a ritual, but a profound way to hold a spiritual vision for your inner being and to passionately seek a state of enlightenment, rather than allowing yourself to live in a state of suffering that propels you toward addiction.\n\nThe teaching is very clear on how to approach this. If you feel you have an addiction or are struggling with a bad habit, you are encouraged to hold that prayer and intention, and to take Deeksha regularly. This involves seeking out a "Deeksha giver," who is a change maker, or a "mitra," who can give you Deeksha.\n\nThe specific instruction is to take Deeksha from someone regularly for over 49 days, every day. This consistent, dedicated practice is seen as a way to continuously work on yourself, elevate your consciousness, and grow. It helps you move beyond a selfish consciousness and connect with a greater purpose, making it much more difficult to succumb to the pull of addiction.\n\nRemember, freedom is not a one-day or one-week affair. It is a continuous journey of work and growth. By approaching Deeksha with passion and staying in touch with the community, you are actively choosing to push yourself upward and not degenerate. It is a beautiful way to connect with the support available to you on your path.\n\nI am unable to find specific teachings on this topic.\n\n*(Teachings referenced: oneness blessing, frontal lobe, parietal)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y9iL10DPhzI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EpReLy7g6WM", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-19 12:24:29+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tier": "fast", "m