ec0b892d-f10f-4421-8bd4-aeeb18d652da	c5100a38-5991-4980-8279-922381389ea2	That's a beautiful and very specific question. It touches on the heart of how we experience life, even in simple things like eating.\n\nThe teachings of Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji don't focus on the specific food, like pizza, but on the quality of our awareness while we eat. The question isn't really about the pizza, but about the state of our mind and body in that moment.\n\nThe core teaching is to let our awareness be our master. We are taught to feel how our body feels after eating. If the food makes us feel heavy and drowsy, it's not for us. If it makes us feel light and awake, then it is for us. The goal is to cultivate a beautiful state where we are present and clear, not weighed down.\n\nSo, if we were to apply this to your question, we would ask: "How does that pizza make me feel?" Does it leave me feeling light and present, or heavy and sleepy? The beautiful state is one of clarity and presence, and that is what we cultivate in every moment, including the simple act of eating. It is this quality of awareness, this beautiful state of being, that is the true nourishment, regardless of what is on the plate.\n\nI am unable to find specific teachings on whether Sri Krishnaji eats pizza. However, the principles from their teachings can guide us in understanding the state of our own being.\n\nWatch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ffhDTzE4nDU", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-19 12:41:57+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tier": "fast", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ffhDTzE4nDU", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA"], "model_provider": "sarvam_cloud", "route_decision": "fast",