b30aaa8d-4d10-4d8e-b368-ef57fa10be72	77fa76ec-35d9-458a-9e99-41eac8430c97	I hear your question, and it comes from a place of deep compassion, seeking a lasting and permanent solution to suffering. It is a very natural and important question to ask.\n\nLooking at the teachings from Sri Preethaji, the focus is often on the profound and powerful nature of Deeksha. The text describes Deeksha as a divine phenomenon that, when many people give it together, can invite immeasurable grace to heal the planet of this disease. This speaks to a collective, powerful healing that has the potential to transform our world.\n\nHowever, the teachings also guide us to understand that the ultimate purpose of Deeksha is to help us experience the 'Enlightenment State.' It's not just about a temporary fix, but about a fundamental shift in our perception. From that state of oneness, where there is no separation, the very idea of 'disease' as a permanent, personal problem can be seen differently.\n\nSo, while Deeksha holds the incredible potential to heal and transform, the teaching points towards a deeper, more permanent freedom that comes from awakening to the divine within, rather than just a cure for a condition. It is a journey of awakening, where the healing is a natural consequence of realizing our true, limitless nature.\n\nI am unable to find specific teachings on this topic.\n\n*(Teachings referenced: oneness blessing, frontal lobe, parietal)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_KtWOkUsy1w", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=md0y8j1SxBk", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-19 12:49:20+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tier": "fast", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_KtWOkUsy1w", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=md0y8j1SxBk"], "model_provider": "sarvam_cloud", "route_decision": "fast", "routing_reason": "pre_