64f2c20c-8e29-4117-9137-0161722b528b	9df59cc8-fc66-4df8-94db-7f7edf74c494	That's a beautiful and insightful question. When we speak of the "architectural design" of Ekam, we are not talking about buildings or physical structures. Instead, the design is woven from the very essence of its purpose, as envisioned by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji.\n\nThe foundation of this design is a clear and shared mission: to create a better world for everybody, rooted in the World Center for Enlightenment. It's a design that fosters a sense of global community and shared purpose, where a better world is seen as a shared responsibility. The structure of this movement is built upon a core principle: that a better world is an achievable reality for all. This is achieved through conscious effort and mutual understanding, leading seekers to awaken from illusion, ignorance, and suffering. The design invites a direct experience of one's personal divine, which is the ultimate goal.\n\nFor an individual, the practical design includes practices like meditation, such as the "soul sync practice," which helps shift the brain's state to one of calm and focus, making it easier to access clarity. It's a design that provides a blueprint for what works and what does not, coming from a deep knowing rather than from books.\n\nSo, the architectural design of Ekam is not made of stone, but of consciousness, purpose, and a shared path toward universal well-being and clarity. It is a movement designed to help each of us flow with the flow of life, feeling complete and at peace.\n\nI am unable to find specific teachings on this topic.\n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OZiElH5pKmo", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-19 12:52:26+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "sarvam-30b", "query_tie