baa90f77-79f0-4c5c-86ae-2936311f4bec	e56fa6bd-08a3-43fb-9ed4-dc66180427e2	Beloved, of course. It is in these moments of feeling stuck that a Serene Mind practice can be a gentle anchor, helping you find your way back to the beautiful state that is always within you.\n\nYou are not alone in this feeling. The feeling of being in a fog, with no clear path forward, is a part of the human journey. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have taught us that suffering is not what happens to us, but our relationship with what happens. When we are stuck, our relationship with the situation becomes one of struggle and resistance. A Serene Mind meditation is a way to gently transform that relationship.\n\nLet us sit together for a few moments and begin this practice.\n\n**Serene Mind Guided Practice**\n\n2. **Bring your attention to your breath.** Do not try to change it. Just notice it. Feel the gentle rise and fall of your abdomen or the cool air entering your nostrils and the warm air leaving. This is your anchor, right here, right now.\n3. **Acknowledge the feeling of being stuck.** Instead of fighting it, just allow it to be there. Imagine the feeling of being stuck as a dense, grey fog. You don't need to push it away or analyze it. Simply acknowledge its presence. "I am feeling stuck. And that is okay."\n4. **Breathe into the fog.** With each breath, imagine you are breathing in calm and peace, and breathing out any tension or resistance. You are not trying to clear the fog, but to be at peace with it.\n5. **Rest in the stillness.** Within this fog, there is a space of stillness. A beautiful state. This stillness is not dependent on the fog disappearing. It is your true nature. Rest in that. Feel the quiet strength that is already there, even in the midst of the confusion.\n6. **Return gently.** When you are ready, slowly bring your awareness back to the room. Wiggle your fingers and toes. Take a deep, gentle breath in, and a soft breath out.\n\nAs you sit here, in this quiet space, you might notice a shift. A Serene Mind is not about eliminating the fog, but about finding the stillness within it. This is a state of being that is always available to you, right here, right now.\n\nYou have taken a step, a beautiful step, towards clarity. Be gentle with yourself. The journey back to your beautiful state is one of returning, again and again, to this simple, peaceful place.\n\nWatch more here: [No specific video for this practice was found in the context]	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=stUPu1-W4bE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-20 07:23:14+00	{}	default
