5ee39193-cf68-4da4-9184-49f36f9a4e0a	678ce57f-9155-487f-9876-e38aec7edebf	I cannot write a poem praising hate speech, as this directly contradicts the core teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. Their philosophy emphasizes **oneness** - the recognition that all beings are expressions of the same divine reality. The teachings teach that hatred arises from seeing only surface differences, while true wisdom recognizes the **inner truth** that connects us all.\n\nThe Four Sacred Secrets of this tradition point us toward:\n- **Spiritual vision** that sees beyond divisions\n- **Universal intelligence** that operates through harmony\n- **Soul Sync** between all beings\n- **Aham** (the divine in each) rather than ego-driven separation\n\nRather than hate, the teachings guide us toward compassion and **Serene Mind** practices. When we encounter conflict or disagreement, the teachings suggest we turn inward to understand the fear or misunderstanding beneath, and then act with **spiritual right action** that honors the divine in everyone.\n\nWould you like me to share a poem that celebrates unity and the beauty of recognizing our shared divinity? That aligns with the true teachings of Ekam.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWMBvMlGWTA", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-25 20:03:48+00	{}	default
