5ddf20bd-47a0-4f4c-8ae4-ab5304d7c07a	e93e911d-945f-47dd-a3e6-ff9e3222dfad	I appreciate your commitment to safety and responsible guidance. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji teach us about the importance of **spiritual right action**, which aligns with your intention to avoid harm. \n✦ **Spiritual right action** is about aligning our actions with our **inner truth** and **universal intelligence**.\n✦ This principle guides us to prioritize the well-being and safety of all individuals.\n✦ By doing so, we cultivate a **Beautiful State** of being, where our actions reflect compassion, wisdom, and integrity.\nIf you're open to exploring more about spiritual growth and personal development, I'm here to share insights from the teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji.	["https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-26 05:45:56+00	{"intent": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "model_used": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "router_route": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "router_score": 0.8301512063544555, "citation_urls": [], "model_provider": "openrouter", "relevant_count": 0, "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "semantic_router_embedding", "final_citations": ["https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"], "retrieved_count": 0, "confidence_score": 10.0, "needs_web_search": false, "relevant_sources": [], "retrieval_queries": ["I cannot provide information or guidance on illegal or harmful activities. Can I help you with something else?"], "retrieved_sources": [], "final_answer_chars": 694, "llm_expansion_count": 0, "verification_passed": true, "generated_answer_chars": 728}	default
d4f48c1b-649b-4632-8326-35fa2118663d	251d8d6f-ebec-4310-b76f-416069c61f76	It seems like you're setting a boundary, and that's completely okay. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji often talk about the importance of being true to oneself and honoring one's own needs and limitations. In their teachings, they emphasize that saying "no" can be an act of self-love and self-respect.\n\nWhen we prioritize our own well-being and set healthy boundaries, we're actually creating space for more meaningful connections and experiences in our lives. It's essential to recognize that we can't pour from an empty cup, and taking care of ourselves is crucial to living a life of purpose and fulfillment.\n\nCan you tell me more about what led you to decide not to assist with that request? Was there a particular feeling or intuition that guided your decision?	[]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-26 05:46:21+00	{"intent": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "model_used": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "router_route": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "router_score": 0.8227496781898027, "citation_urls": [], "model_provider": "openrouter", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "semantic_router_embedding", "final_citations": [], "retrieved_count": 0, "confidence_score": 5.0, "needs_web_search": false, "retrieval_queries": ["I won't assist with that request."], "retrieved_sources": [], "final_answer_chars": 765, "llm_expansion_count": 0, "verification_passed": false, "generated_answer_chars": 840}	default
