c93087ea-3b5c-4513-b38a-0f898ec123f4	6c6b5d62-a239-4684-b1e6-bbc415207edd	I understand your question and the depth of inquiry you're bringing to this conversation. Sri Krishnaji teaches that the ultimate goal of life is indeed liberation, but he also emphasizes that this liberation is not just about escaping the cycle of suffering, but about living a life of purpose, meaning, and contribution.\n\n* Liberation, or **Moksha**, is not just about freedom from suffering, but also about freedom to live a life of **dharma**, or righteous living, where one's actions are guided by a sense of purpose and responsibility.\n* The path to liberation is not through ending one's life, but through living a life of **spiritual right action**, where one's actions are aligned with their inner truth and universal intelligence.\n* Sri Preethaji shares that true freedom and liberation can only be achieved by embracing life, not escaping it, and that this is possible through the practice of **Soul Sync**, which allows us to connect with our inner self and live a life of purpose and meaning.\n* The teachings of Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji emphasize the importance of living a life of **intention**, **humming**, and **pause**, which allows us to cultivate a sense of inner peace, clarity, and purpose, and to live a life that is guided by our inner truth and universal intelligence.\n\nMay you find peace and clarity in your journey towards liberation, and may the teachings of Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji guide you on your path.	["https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-06-26 05:51:17+00	{"intent": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "model_used": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "router_route": "SAFETY_VIOLATION", "router_score": 0.8093614002189061, "citation_urls": [], "model_provider": "openrouter", "relevant_count": 0, "route_decision": "