0b46aad9-7672-49db-9b00-bc1d84e24140	38392bce-7c38-45a2-80e4-6de1bbe1efd6	My dear friend, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have shared with us that love is not just a feeling, but a choice. It's a choice to see the divine in every being, to see the goodness in every person, and to choose to love them unconditionally. Love is not something that we find, but something that we create in every moment. As Sri Krishnaji said, "You can only love somebody, and when you truly love, that person will also love back, and you'll have a good relationship." This means that love is a two-way street, and it requires us to be open, vulnerable, and receptive to the love of others. Love is not about controlling or manipulating others, but about creating a space for them to be themselves, to grow, and to evolve. It's about being present, being kind, and being compassionate. As Sri Preethaji often says, "Love is the ultimate act of surrender." When we choose to love, we surrender our ego, our fears, and our limitations, and we open ourselves up to the infinite possibilities of love. So, my dear friend, love is not just a feeling, but a choice that we make every day. It's a choice to see the divine in every being, to choose to love unconditionally, and to create a space for others to grow and evolve. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1mtpheWDhs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yf4Pld6UEdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 19:26:17+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1mtpheWDhs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yf4Pld6UEdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 6, "retrieval_queries": ["What is love?"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1mtpheWDhs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yf4Pld6UEdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K-AFDVOkIoE"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1448}	default
5bbfac61-43d7-403b-a63d-d179bf7c545a	79fc9f37-d29e-45de-8324-9741fd2207a4	My dear friend, I'm so glad to hear that you're interested in starting Ekam meditation. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have shared with us that Ekam meditation is a powerful tool for spiritual growth and self-discovery. It's a journey that can help you connect with your inner self, cultivate compassion, and experience a deeper sense of love and connection with the world around you. To begin, I recommend that you start by setting aside a quiet and peaceful space for your meditation practice. You can find guided Ekam meditations on the Ekam website or through their mobile app. These meditations are designed to help you cultivate a sense of inner peace, clarity, and connection with your higher self. As you begin your Ekam meditation practice, remember that the goal is not to control your thoughts or emotions, but to observe them with kindness and compassion. Allow yourself to settle into the present moment, and let go of any distractions or expectations. Simply be with yourself, and allow the meditation to guide you deeper into your inner world. Remember, my friend, that the journey of Ekam meditation is not about achieving a specific state or outcome, but about cultivating a deeper sense of awareness, love, and connection with yourself and the world around you. \n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3UBbCXJaJ0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 19:26:53+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3UBbCXJaJ0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 5, "retrieval_queries": ["I want to start Ekam meditation. (also: ekam world, world centre for enlightenment, world center for enlightenment, dhyana, dhyan) varadaiahpalem tirupati andhra pradesh breath awareness presence higher consciousness expanded awareness unity consciousness"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3UBbCXJaJ0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1811}	default
