43c14fd8-e24c-4731-9cc2-cf448d34fc27	d99abf20-dbf2-4275-9d99-0cced9ce389b	My dear friend, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have shared with us that love is not just a feeling, but a choice. It's a choice to see the divine in every being, to see the goodness in every person, and to choose to love them unconditionally. Love is not something that we find, but something that we create in every moment. As Sri Krishnaji said, "You can only love somebody, and when you truly love, that person will also love back, and you'll have a good relationship." This means that love is a two-way street, and it requires us to be open, vulnerable, and receptive to the love of others. Love is not about controlling or manipulating others, but about creating a space for them to be themselves, to grow, and to evolve. It's about being present, being kind, and being compassionate. As Sri Preethaji often says, "Love is the ultimate act of surrender." When we choose to love, we surrender our ego, our fears, and our limitations, and we open ourselves up to the infinite possibilities of love. So, my dear friend, love is not just a feeling, but a choice that we make every day. It's a choice to see the divine in every being, to choose to love unconditionally, and to create a space for others to grow and evolve. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1mtpheWDhs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yf4Pld6UEdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-01 19:39:52+00	{}	default
