9a5659ee-75ca-4fe2-bbf4-0b3079c4cb72	56225488-d587-4a02-b45c-2ce561af84fb	My dear friend, I'm glad you asked about the concept of a "beautiful state." According to the teachings, a "beautiful state" refers to a state of existence where one is free from suffering and lives in a state of enlightenment. This is not just a mental state, but a way of living life completely and fully, unencumbered by the past. In this state, one is not just focused on spiritual abundance, but also experiences financial and social abundance. This is a unique aspect of the teaching, as some spiritual paths may focus solely on spiritual growth, neglecting the practical aspects of life. The beautiful state is a reflection of the inner experience, where one's thoughts and perceptions are aligned with their life. It's a state where one's relationships, work, and overall well-being are all influenced by this inner state of being. In contrast, ordinary consciousness is often characterized by a sense of separation, suffering, and being stuck in the past. The beautiful state, on the other hand, is a state of unity, freedom, and living life in the present moment. \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["unknown"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		10.0	2026-07-01 20:14:04+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgQV_5FjPNk"], "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 1, "reranked_count": 1, "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "heuristic_simple", "retrieved_count": 6, "relevant_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgQV_5FjPNk"], "reranked_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgQV_5FjPNk"], "retrieval_queries": ["Explain the concept of 'beautiful state' according to the teachings of the masters, and how it differs from ordinary consciousness."], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b-MkLkpTeVY", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgQV_5FjPNk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KTlY-lHs_Ew"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1652}	default
a99b1ed8-455c-4b75-801f-9ceacb42adb3	61d881ba-7f48-42fd-942c-b505a025c9ba	My dear friend, I'm so glad to hear that you're interested in starting Ekam meditation. This beautiful practice, as taught by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, is a powerful tool for cultivating inner peace, clarity, and connection with the divine. As you begin your Ekam journey, remember that the key is to approach it with an open heart and mind. Allow yourself to let go of any expectations or preconceptions, and simply be present with the practice. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji often remind us that Ekam is not just a meditation technique, but a way of living. It's about embracing the present moment, just as it is, and finding the beauty in the simplicity of life. As you start your practice, take a few moments to set your intention. Ask yourself, "What is it that I want to cultivate in my life through Ekam meditation?" Is it greater peace, clarity, or connection with the divine? Whatever your intention, remember that Ekam is a journey, not a destination. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3UBbCXJaJ0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 20:14:22+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3UBbCXJaJ0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_l2RNcSPPA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 5, "retrieval_queries": ["I want to start Ekam meditation. (also: ekam world, world centre for enlightenment, world center for enlightenment, dhyana, dh