e11583e0-2e75-40ed-91f8-fea10685d226	3ad00e11-6922-4674-94d1-8dc87195cd4b	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in the Serene Mind practice. This practice is a beautiful way to cultivate inner peace and clarity in your life. As Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji share in their teachings, the Serene Mind practice is a powerful tool to quiet the mind and connect with your inner self. To practice the Serene Mind, you'll need to find a quiet and comfortable place to sit, where you can focus without distractions. Close your eyes and take a few deep breaths, feeling the air move in and out of your body. Now, let's begin the practice:\n\n1. **Focus on your breath**: Bring your attention to your breath, feeling the sensation of the air moving in and out of your nostrils. When your mind wanders, gently bring it back to your breath without judgment. 2. **Notice your thoughts**: As you breathe, notice any thoughts that arise in your mind. Don't try to engage with them or push them away; simply observe them as they pass through your awareness. 3. **Let go of attachment**: Recognize that your thoughts are just thoughts, and they don't define your true nature. Let go of attachment to any particular thought or emotion, and allow yourself to simply be present. 4. **Cultivate awareness**: As you continue to breathe, cultivate awareness of your body and surroundings. Notice any sensations, sounds, or smells that arise, but don't get caught up in them. 5. **Embody the Serene Mind**: Imagine yourself as a calm and peaceful being, radiating serenity and clarity. Feel the weight of your body on the ground, and the sensation of the air moving through your body. 6. **Rest in the present moment**: Allow yourself to rest in the present moment, without judgment or attachment. Simply be, and let go of any need to do or achieve. As you practice the Serene Mind, remember that the goal is not to achieve a specific state, but to cultivate awareness and acceptance of the present moment. With regular practice, you'll find that your mind becomes quieter, and you'll experience greater clarity and inner peace. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gv3w2uNCo2o", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jK7-PPBXwr4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 20:16:13+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gv3w2uNCo2o", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jK7-PPBXwr4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 3, "retrieval_queries": ["What is the Serene Mind practice and what are the detailed steps to practice it?"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jK7-PPBXwr4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gv3w2uNCo2o"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 2298}	default
