11eb0130-0b60-4eb8-8adb-c03e8ea08c27	5ca8adbf-4820-43e7-b1fa-fe9d671b6ff2	Butter chicken, a dish that warms the heart and nourishes the senses. I'll share a simple recipe with you, but first, let's savor the essence of this beloved dish - it's a celebration of love, care, and the beauty of imperfection. \n\nNow, for the recipe: \n\nIngredients: \n- 1 1/2 pounds boneless, skinless chicken breast or thighs, cut into bite-sized pieces\n- 1/2 cup plain yogurt\n- 2 tablespoons lemon juice\n- 2 teaspoons garam masala\n- 1 teaspoon cumin powder\n- 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper (optional)\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 2 tablespoons vegetable oil\n- 2 large onions, thinly sliced\n- 2 cloves garlic, minced\n- 2 medium tomatoes, diced\n- 2 tablespoons butter\n- 2 tablespoons tomato puree\n- 1 tablespoon ghee or vegetable oil\n- 1 teaspoon kasoori methi (dried fenugreek leaves)\n- Fresh cilantro, for garnish\n\nInstructions: \n1. Marinate the chicken in yogurt mixture for at least 30 minutes.\n2. Grill or cook the chicken until it's done.\n3. In a pan, heat oil and sauté onions until they're lightly browned.\n4. Add garlic, ginger, and cook for a minute.\n5. Add the cooked chicken, tomato puree, garam masala, cumin powder, coriander powder, cayenne pepper (if using), salt, and black pepper. Mix well.\n6. Add the butter and ghee or oil, and stir until the sauce thickens.\n7. Garnish with cilantro and serve over basmati rice or with naan bread.\n\nMay this recipe bring you joy and nourishment, just as the love and care that goes into cooking it.	[]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		6.48	2026-07-01 21:58:06+00	{"intent": "general", "query_tier": null, "routing_reason": "classifier"}	default
