e38292b8-1df1-4c90-a9d1-f9bbea07a3b7	fb77af67-afb5-4279-ac07-8d59108e7fa2	My child, it seems we've taken a detour from our beautiful conversation about the Serene Mind practice. Let's gently bring our attention back to the present moment and the teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. The Serene Mind practice is a powerful tool for returning to calm and clarity whenever we're distracted or preoccupied. Remember, it's three minutes to a serene state of mind. Let's focus on deepening our understanding of this practice. When we're in a stressful state, our mind is often entangled in the past or future. We're preoccupied with thoughts of what's lacking or what's gone wrong. But what if we could shift our attention to the present moment? What if we could cultivate a sense of connection and love, rather than being caught up in our own thoughts and emotions? The Serene Mind practice helps us do just that. By focusing on our breath, recognizing our emotions, and moving our attention to the eyebrow center, we can begin to let go of our attachment to thoughts and emotions. We can start to see the world from a different perspective, one that's filled with love, compassion, and connection. So, my child, let's not get caught up in external distractions, like the idea of a secret gold mine. Instead, let's focus on cultivating a sense of inner peace and clarity. Let's practice the Serene Mind and see how it can transform our lives. Watch more here:, \n\n*(Teachings referenced: Ekam, world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.breathingroom.com/", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 21:59:14+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decisi