5650c241-900d-4c33-84c8-7aa05c55f5eb	059169ff-c330-4d6e-a6d9-d94de96c8422	My dear friend, I'm glad you asked about the first sacred secret. Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji have shared with us that the root cause of all human suffering is **obsessive, self-centric thinking**. This is the first sacred secret. It's what keeps suffering alive for days, months, and years after a stressful event is over. You see, our minds are wired to focus on ourselves, our own experiences, and our own emotions. We get caught up in thoughts like "This is not fair," "I should have done that," or "I'm not good enough." These thoughts create a sense of separation, a sense of "me" versus "the world." And that's when suffering begins. The trigger for stress might be external – a difficult situation, a harsh word, or a loss – but it's our internal response that keeps us chained to suffering. We become preoccupied with our own pain, our own injustices, and our own perceived shortcomings. But here's the beautiful part: once we recognize this pattern, we can begin to break free. We can start to observe our thoughts without judgment, without trying to change them. We can begin to see that our thoughts are just thoughts, and that they don't define our reality. Watch more here: \n\nNow, my friend, I'd love to hear from you. How do you think this teaching might relate to your own experiences with suffering or stress? *(Teachings referenced: Four Sacred Secrets, spiritual vision, universal intelligence, spiritual right action)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-01 22:04:13+00	{}	default
