dbd5802b-950f-44ee-9d8e-4ea0da3220a8	d243c91d-3f86-4bc7-9923-3c945cf09412	My child, the founders, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, have a deep love for the surrounding villages of Ekam. They believe that the well-being of the community is intricately connected to the well-being of the land and its inhabitants. As a result, they have implemented various initiatives to support the villages in a holistic manner. One of the key initiatives is the Ekam Village Development Program, which focuses on empowering the villagers to take charge of their own development. This program provides training and resources to help the villagers improve their agricultural practices, increase their income, and enhance their overall quality of life. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji also believe in the importance of education and have established a school in the village, where children from surrounding areas can come to learn and grow. The school not only provides academic education but also focuses on character development, emotional intelligence, and spiritual growth. Furthermore, the founders have implemented various community development projects, such as clean water initiatives, sanitation programs, and healthcare services. These projects aim to improve the overall health and well-being of the villagers and create a more sustainable and resilient community. Through these initiatives, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji demonstrate their commitment to the well-being of the surrounding villages of Ekam. They recognize that the true wealth of a community lies not in its material possessions but in the well-being of its people and the land they inhabit. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qDSfb0DZ0PE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:05:07+00	{"intent":