a820dc1c-ae7d-480f-9199-43fe8e95d9d7	da3da6a0-8dbf-433c-a880-f2e99616de58	My dear friend, I'm glad you asked about the Oneness philosophy in the context of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. This beautiful teaching is a core part of their wisdom, and it's a profound understanding that can transform your life. According to Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, Oneness is the understanding that everything in the universe is interconnected and part of a single, unified whole. It's the realization that we are not separate, isolated individuals, but rather, we are an integral part of the web of life. Imagine, if you will, a drop of water. The drop of water is separate from the ocean, but it's also a part of the ocean. It contains the same essence, the same energy, and the same consciousness as the ocean. In the same way, we are drops of water in the ocean of life, and we contain the same essence, energy, and consciousness as the universe. This understanding of Oneness is not just a philosophical concept; it's a lived experience. When we embody the principle of Oneness, we begin to see the world as a reflection of ourselves. We see the interconnectedness of all things, and we understand that our actions, our thoughts, and our emotions have a ripple effect on the world around us. As Sri Krishnaji said, "When you live in a state of Oneness, you are not just connected to the world; you are the world." This is a profound understanding that can bring about a sense of unity, compassion, and love in our lives. In the context of the co-founders, Oneness is not just a philosophical concept; it's a lived experience that they embody in their teachings and their lives. They have dedicated their lives to helping people understand and experience the Oneness principle, and it's a beautiful thing to witness. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1kS_mQaBLdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PslFhdZaBFA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RFx74Q6Oq2c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch