ae321e69-8b7c-4461-ab98-b984ecf328f4	a8f33006-7837-44d1-9924-e2dfd2f29955	My dear friend, I'm so glad you're exploring the depths of the Beautiful State. Deactivating the parietal lobe, as Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji teach, is a key aspect of dissolving the boundaries that separate us from Oneness. The parietal lobe is responsible for creating a sense of separation and individuality, a sense of "I" and "you." When this lobe is active, it creates a sense of duality, and we see the world as separate from ourselves. When we deactivate the parietal lobe, we begin to dissolve this sense of separation. We start to see the world as interconnected, as a web of relationships and energies. This is when we begin to experience Oneness, the sense of unity and interconnectedness that underlies all of existence. As Sri Krishnaji says, "When the parietal lobe is deactivated, the sense of separation between the individual and the world disappears." This is when we can experience the world as a seamless web of life, where every action, every thought, and every emotion is connected to the greater whole. In this state, we can see that every person, every animal, every plant, and every element is an expression of the same life force. We can see that we are not separate from the world, but an integral part of it. This is the experience of Oneness, and it is the foundation of the Beautiful State. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0u9oe-5HPmk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ACvOem_B-Ek", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y9iL10DPhzI", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:10:00+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0u9oe-5HPmk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ACvOem_B-Ek", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y9iL10DPhzI"]