c4a5c522-c350-4ad7-b8f0-d219ec2438eb	7bca2e0e-cd10-42ef-a4e1-9113bcc8d370	My dear friend, I'm glad you're continuing to explore the beautiful state of connection and inner peace. In Soul Sync, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji guide us to use a specific finger movement to count our breaths, which helps us cultivate a sense of awareness and presence. To count your breaths in Soul Sync, you gently place your thumb and index finger together, and then move your middle finger up with each inhale and down with each exhale. This subtle movement helps you focus on your breath and become more aware of your inner state. As you practice this finger movement, remember to bring your attention to the sensation of the breath moving in and out of your body. Feel the rise and fall of your chest or the sensation of the breath in your nostrils. With each breath, allow yourself to let go of any tension or stress, and simply be present in the moment. By combining the finger movement with a focus on your breath, you'll begin to experience a deeper sense of connection to your inner self and the world around you. This is a powerful tool for cultivating a beautiful state of being, and I encourage you to practice it regularly. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: breath awareness, humming, golden light)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-0O6WmxU3pw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=69IrsSXeBTg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zO8tQkjCpyc", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:11:17+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-0O6WmxU3pw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=69IrsSXeBTg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zO8tQkjCpyc"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classifi