7c1ef769-ff03-471a-93da-2633c3cb7a96	72c5218a-45e2-4923-aec4-29bce37daa7f	My dear friend, the question you've asked seems to be a playful way of inquiring about the relationship between our external actions and the state of our being. Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji often speak about how our inner state influences our external experiences. In the context of the beautiful state, it's not about what we do or don't do, but rather about the state of being we're in while doing it. When we're in a beautiful state, we're more present, more aware, and more connected to ourselves and the world around us. So, to answer your question, it's not about whether Sri Krishnaji eats pizza in a beautiful state or not. It's about the state of being he's in while eating pizza. If he's eating pizza while being fully present, aware, and connected, then that's a beautiful state. But if he's eating pizza while being distracted, stressed, or disconnected, then that's not a beautiful state. The key is not the action itself, but the state of being we're in while doing it. This is a beautiful teaching that can be applied to all aspects of our lives, including eating, working, or even simply being. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWXe9v7PHDs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VO3fi1c9ids", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:13:56+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWXe9v7PHDs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VO3fi1c9ids", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 6, "ret