a1d9417b-16cf-48da-984d-0192eb59d501	b3b9294d-1884-42f5-aa92-655179dc1411	My child, I see that you're seeking to apply the Power of Letting Go to your homework. This is a beautiful intention, as it shows you're willing to release attachment to a specific outcome. However, I must clarify that the Power of Letting Go is not about avoiding responsibilities or tasks, but rather about releasing the emotional charge and attachment to the outcome. When you're feeling overwhelmed by your homework, it's essential to recognize that the stress and anxiety you're experiencing are not the homework itself, but rather your perception of it. By letting go of the attachment to the outcome, you can approach your homework with a sense of curiosity and openness, rather than resistance and stress. Imagine that your homework is a wave, and you're the observer standing on the shore. You can choose to get caught up in the wave's energy, or you can observe it from a distance, allowing it to pass without attachment. This is the essence of the Power of Letting Go. As Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji teach, "When you let go of your attachment to the outcome, you create space for the universe to unfold its plan." By releasing your attachment to the homework, you're creating space for your inner wisdom to guide you, and for the universe to provide the necessary resources and support. So, my child, I encourage you to approach your homework with a sense of curiosity and openness, and to let go of the attachment to the outcome. Remember, the Power of Letting Go is not about avoiding responsibilities, but about releasing the emotional charge and attachment to the outcome. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1kS_mQaBLdg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7lggUuJtZXY", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f-IpkGOOzYU"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:15:13+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used":