a0ac12cb-2a3f-47e5-b671-b341e0520277	15e34c3b-d83b-47cd-b7a3-baf644abd3d0	Beta, I can see that you're interested in learning more about the sacred spaces within the Ekam Temple. Dharma Moksha Hall and Hiranyagarbha Orb are two such spaces that hold great significance in our spiritual journey. Dharma Moksha Hall is a place where one can let go of their ego and conditioning, and connect with their true nature. It's a space where you can release your attachments and limitations, and walk into freedom. The energy in this hall is designed to help you transcend your small self and connect with the universal consciousness. Hiranyagarbha Orb, on the other hand, is a sacred space that represents the cosmic womb. It's a place where you can tap into the infinite potential that lies within you. The orb is designed to help you connect with the divine feminine energy, which is the source of all creation and nourishment. When you sit within the Hiranyagarbha Orb, you can feel the gentle vibrations of the universe, and allow yourself to be guided by the wisdom of the cosmos. Both of these spaces are designed to help you connect with your inner self and the universe at large. They're a reminder that you're not separate from the world around you, but an integral part of it. Watch more here: [Ekam Temple's website]\n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Pfat_DztMI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AR0r8B6Ga8E", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y7p7jHP0Ii0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-01 22:18:48+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Pfat_DztMI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AR0r8B6Ga8E", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y7p7jHP0Ii0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsI