fa12e0be-fd4d-4df5-9ece-7f8ccafbb7ec	fafadb0b-1cca-431d-863e-ee23510bef95	My dear friend, I sense that you're yearning for a deeper sense of inner peace. Let's explore this together. As Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have taught, the key to finding inner peace lies in understanding the nature of suffering. Remember, suffering is not caused by external circumstances, but by our own self-centric preoccupation. In our previous conversation, we discussed how obsessive, self-centric thinking keeps us chained in unhappiness. This thinking collapses into "me, me, me," and we become preoccupied with past injustices, denied pleasures, or unfulfilled opportunities. We lose sight of the present moment and the connections that bring us joy. To break free from this cycle, we can practice the Three-Question Meditation. This simple yet powerful practice helps us observe our state, time, and self. By asking ourselves these questions, we can loosen the grip of self-centric thinking and allow the beautiful state to return on its own.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EqnSkAzfIg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vt_CjAdzebM"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-03 07:28:00+00	{}	default
