b5e5aa0c-1874-4f1d-a14e-e2eb0c1e33b3	0e77fb77-bfe7-46fa-9541-965fac1881c4	Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji offer guidance on moving from suffering to a beautiful state. **Beautiful State** is a state of connection, peace, and inner joy, free from suffering. According to Sri Krishnaji, immersing in the state of Mahashanti during a Deeksha experience can be a starting point for transformation. This experience is meant to help you connect with the inner state and move away from suffering. For daily practices, Sri Preethaji recommends the **Three-Question Meditation**, which is a short practice that helps you connect with your inner self. This meditation is not about a specific religion but about being human and returning to a beautiful state. Additionally, Sri Krishnaji shares the **Serene Mind** practice, a 3-minute practice to return to calm whenever you feel distracted, disturbed, or preoccupied with past or future. This practice can help you move from a suffering state to a beautiful state. It's essential to note that Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji emphasize the importance of being aware of your inner state and living with the awareness of the state you are in. By doing so, you can move away from states of suffering and immerse in states of no suffering, which can lead to a transformation in your life. \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["unknown", "unknown", "https://www.ekam.org/", "Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "unknown", "unknown", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		5.1	2026-07-05 04:40:18+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier3_complex", "memory_used": false, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWX