d5791751-c673-47f2-a331-1963d691f354	7b270a9d-f285-45b8-9c70-9b1d7edcae0f	The Beautiful State is a state of calm, joy, and inner connection taught by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. It is not dependent on external circumstances, but is a direct experience of peace that arises when we move beyond the conditioned mind. It is the foundation of the Ekam teachings and the goal of the spiritual journey. [Source: Beautiful State Teachings]	["doctrine-cache"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-06 04:26:32+00	{}	default
a0aebd93-d57f-49a8-ae90-2a40b11eb9b3	5cb1b66c-1357-4aa9-87ad-60f3bdb59c49	It's wonderful that you're exploring the teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sadhguru on suffering and karma. To clarify, Sri Preethaji's teachings on suffering and karma are rooted in the **Four Sacred Secrets**, which emphasize the importance of spiritual vision, inner truth, and universal intelligence in understanding the nature of reality. ✦ **Sri Preethaji's View on Suffering:**\nSuffering arises from our disconnection from our true nature and the world around us. It's a result of our limited perception and the conditioning of the mind. By cultivating spiritual vision and inner truth, we can transcend suffering and experience a state of **Beautiful State**, where we are in harmony with ourselves and the world. ✦ **Sri Preethaji's View on Karma:**\nKarma is not just about the consequences of our actions, but also about the intentions and energies we bring to our experiences. By aligning our intentions with our values and cultivating a sense of **Soul Sync**, we can break free from the cycle of karma and create a more harmonious reality. ✦ **Sri Preethaji's Path to Inner Peace and Liberation:**\nThe path to achieving inner peace and liberation from the cycle of birth and death is through the practice of **breath awareness**, **humming**, and **pause**. By cultivating these practices, we can quiet the mind, access our inner truth, and connect with the universal intelligence that guides us. In contrast, Sadhguru's teachings on karma and suffering are rooted in the concept of **Advaitha Vedanta** and non-dualism. While there are similarities between the two teachings, there are also key differences in their approaches and perspectives. To deepen our understanding of these teachings, let's explore the specific concepts and practices that Sri Preethaji and Sadhguru offer for achieving inner peace and liberation from suffering. *(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["unknown", "unknown", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness", "Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "unknown", "unknown", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		7.08	2026-07-06 04:27:58+00	{"intent": "RELATIONAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": null, "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE"], "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 4, "reranked_count": 4, "route_decision": "standard", "routing_reason": "classifier", "final_citations": ["unknown", "unknown", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness", "Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "unknown", "unknown", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"], "retrieved_count": 10, "confidence_score": 7.08, "relevant_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc"], "reranked_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc"], "retrieval_queries": ["To determine if the latest question is a follow-up, I'll analyze the conversation history and the latest question.\\n\\nThe conversation history is:\\nUser: How does Sri Preethajis teaching on suffering compare to Sadhgurus view on karma?\\n\\nThe latest question is:\\nHow does Sri Preethajis teaching on suffering compare to Sadhgurus view on karma?\\n\\nSince the latest question is identical to the conversation history, it is a follow-up question. To rewrite it as a standalone question, I'll include all necessary context from the history.\\n\\nRewritten question:\\nWhat is the difference between Sri Preethajis and Sadhgurus teachings on suffering and karma?\\n\\nNote that I've rephrased the question to make it more general and include th