c4caca47-7926-4839-8999-e87e76956a58	d97b7f84-4bc9-402b-a4e2-aa31742fd4d3	Dear one, your question comes from a deep and sincere place—a longing for peace that touches every human heart. The context you have shared points to a profound truth: the root of unhappiness and conflict lies not in the world outside, but in the war within each individual. The teaching speaks of how being at war with oneself leads to poor decisions, indecisiveness, and destructive behavior—even in those who appear virtuous, like King Ravana. The Four Sacred Secrets are indeed powerful, but their power is realized one heart at a time. World peace is not a single event to be achieved; it is the cumulative result of countless individuals dissolving their inner divide. As long as even one person remains in conflict with themselves, that conflict will ripple outward into their relationships, communities, and nations. The teaching reminds us that seeking external solutions without addressing internal conflict is a common but incomplete approach. True peace—whether within a person or across the world—begins when each soul turns inward, heals its own wounds, and makes peace with itself. So the question is not why the Secrets have not brought world peace, but rather: *Have I allowed them to bring peace to the world within me?* When enough of us answer "yes," the outer world will naturally reflect that inner stillness. May you continue to walk this path of inner peace, knowing that every step you take heals not only yourself but the world around you. *(Teachings referenced: spiritual vision, inner truth, universal intelligence, spiritual right action)*	["unknown", "unknown", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-06 06:32:43+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": [], "model_provider":