70f25d74-4c94-4aac-9537-141c44e7037f	27bba1a4-1390-49bb-9c1f-5ed31d2b0321	Dear one, I understand your question. It is a very common experience, and there is no need to feel discouraged. In the teachings of Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji, when they guide you to visualize a flame—as in the Serene Mind practice or the Three-Question Meditation—they often say *“visualize or feel.”* This is a gentle invitation, not a demand for perfect mental imagery. If you do not see anything, simply shift your attention to *feeling* the presence of the flame. You can sense its warmth, its light, or simply intend that it is there. The essence of the practice is not the clarity of the image, but the movement of your awareness from the thinking mind to a quiet, centered space. Even a subtle sense of “I am holding my attention here” is enough. Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have taught that the flame is a symbol of your own inner light. Whether you see it, sense it, or only imagine it, the act of turning inward with a gentle smile already begins to dissolve the grip of stress and distraction. So please, do not judge yourself. Simply continue with the practice, allowing whatever arises—or does not arise—to be exactly as it is. You are already on the path. Trust the process, and let the practice unfold in its own time.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	0.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-06 06:33:12+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18"], "model_provider": "ollama", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 9, "retrieval_queries": ["What if I don't see anything when I visualize?"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMc_kat7YLE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0u9oe-