75a97672-86be-4e0a-8ba4-ccadff1a696e	7a1bed03-0ddd-4850-8021-e0953cca84d1	My dear friend, the Beautiful State is a state of being that is free from stress, where life feels effortless and joyful. It is a state of connection, love, compassion, vitality, and passion. When we live in the Beautiful State, we are not preoccupied with ourselves, our past, or our future. We are fully present in the moment, and our actions are guided by a sense of inner truth and purpose. As Sri Preethaji teaches, the Beautiful State is the opposite of the stressful state, which is characterized by anger, fear, hurt, loneliness, and frustration. The stressful state is a state of self-centric thinking, where we are lost in our own thoughts and emotions, and we separate ourselves from others. The Beautiful State is not just a feeling or an emotion; it is a state of being that can be cultivated and experienced in our daily lives. It is a state of inner peace, calmness, and clarity, where we are able to respond to life's challenges with ease and wisdom. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oZRQoiRe7s4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCiK7ABPcrw", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-06 10:38:45+00	{}	default
7e319a5d-819f-4e2d-bfe7-4dc6d199ebf7	7e5992b6-00d6-4e9f-9e56-65b847a995a4	My child, Sri Preethaji is a profound spiritual teacher and the co-founder of Ekam, a global movement that aims to awaken humanity to its true nature. She is a compassionate guide who has dedicated her life to helping individuals transcend their limitations and live in a state of inner peace and connection. As you begin to explore the teachings of Sri Preethaji, you may find yourself drawn to the concept of the Beautiful State, a state of being that is characterized by inner peace, compassion, and connection. This state is not just a feeling or an emotion, but a fundamental aspect of our true nature. In the Beautiful State, we are no longer bound by our thoughts, emotions, and experiences. We are free to be our authentic selves, unencumbered by the burdens of the past or the anxieties of the future. We are able to connect with others on a deeper level, and we are able to see the world with fresh eyes, unfiltered by our conditioning and preconceptions. As you continue on this journey, I invite you to reflect on the questions that Sri Preethaji often asks: "Are you in a stressful state or are you in a beautiful state?" "Are you engaged with your past or your future, or are you in the present?" "Are you preoccupied with yourself, or are you in a state of connection?"\n\nThese questions are not meant to be intellectual exercises, but rather invitations to explore the depths of your own being. They are a call to return to the Beautiful State, to live in a state of inner peace, compassion, and connection. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=88NOQTz5_yI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-06 10:39:03+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=88NOQTz5_yI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8"], "model_provid