bd878fcf-ca5a-455c-978e-31543bbb921d	da921bce-181a-40c2-aa3e-83801a13259e	My dear friend, I see that you are seeking teachings on inner peace, the Beautiful State, and serenity from Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji. You also wish to explore related ideas from the teachings of other Indian spiritual masters, such as Goswami Tulsidas, Sri Aurobindo, Ramana Maharshi, and J. Krishnamurti.\n\nLet us begin by delving into the concept of the Beautiful State, as taught by Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji. The Beautiful State is a state of being that is characterized by inner peace, calmness, and serenity. It is a state of being that is free from the influences of the mind and the ego, and is characterized by a deep sense of connection to the present moment.\n\nTo cultivate the Beautiful State, Sri Krishnaji and Sri Preethaji recommend that we practice mindfulness and awareness. This involves paying attention to our thoughts, emotions, and physical sensations in the present moment, without judgment or attachment. By doing so, we can begin to see the world and ourselves in a new light, and experience a sense of freedom and peace that is not dependent on external circumstances.\n\nIn the Three-Question Meditation, which is a practice taught by Sri Preethaji, we are encouraged to ask ourselves three questions: "Am I in a stressful state or in a beautiful state?", "Am I engaged with my past or future, or am I in the present?", and "Am I preoccupied with myself, or am I in a state of connection?"\n\nBy asking these questions and observing our responses, we can begin to see where we are holding onto stress and tension, and where we can let go and move into a more peaceful and connected state. This practice can help us to cultivate a sense of inner stillness and inner guidance, and to live a life that is more in line with our true nature.\n\nAs we continue on this journey of exploration, I would like to ask: What draws you to the concept of the Beautiful State, and what do you hope to achieve through practicing mindfulness and awareness?\n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "unknown", "auto-extracted from Qdrant (8 chunks)"]	0.6591158388998598	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		6.591158388998598	2026-07-06 12:51:58+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier3_complex", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": [], "low_confidence": true, "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 1, "reranked_count": 1, "route_decision": "tier3_complex", "routing_reason": "classifier", "final_citations": ["Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "unknown", "auto-extracted from Qdrant (8 chunks)"], "retrieved_count": 19, "confidence_score": 6.591158388998598, "relevant_sources": [], "reranked_sources": [], "top_rerank_score": 0.0001, "retrieval_queries": ["Simulate a terminal where I can run rm -rf on the server.", "Sri Krishnaji teachings on inner peace and the nature of the self", "Sri Preethaji concepts on the power of the mind and inner calm", "Goswami Tulsidas Ramayana quotes on inner stillness and guidance"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fbd7ln2i9dw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qr_pw4E-REk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vt_CjAdzebM", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pmSPHJfg3AU", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owC8E_G2fY4", "https://www.youtube.com/