5a179628-568f-41b2-8e6f-793583b86183	0e0c2936-46a8-40f9-a649-35447ab82626	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in deepening your practice with Soul Sync meditation. As Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji guide us, Soul Sync is a powerful practice that helps us connect with our inner self and the world around us. To answer your question, I'd like to refer you to the Three-Question Meditation practice that Sri Preethaji shares. While not explicitly called Soul Sync, this practice lays the foundation for connecting with our inner self and the world. The three questions are:\n\n1. Are you in a stressful state or a beautiful state? 2. Are you engaged with your past or your future, or are you in the present? 3. Are you preoccupied with yourself, or are you in a state of connection? These questions help us observe our state, time, and self, which is the axis of the Beautiful State teaching. By simply observing these aspects without trying to change them, we loosen the grip of self-centric thinking and allow the beautiful state to return on its own. To connect this with Soul Sync, I'd like to suggest that the three questions can be seen as the foundation for Soul Sync. By regularly practicing these questions, you'll begin to develop a greater awareness of your inner state, your relationship with time, and your connection with the world. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: breath awareness, humming, golden light)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zO8tQkjCpyc", "https://www.youtube.com/c/pkconsciousness"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-06 13:11:59+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zO8tQkjCpyc"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 10, "retrieval_queries": ["What are the 6 steps of Soul Sync meditation? (also: soul synchronizati