32e413b7-45a0-4cdf-b431-9d92652e7e78	17ed3d88-f640-4986-97d7-26c086e8327d	My dear friend, I'm so glad you're interested in exploring the teachings of Sri Preethaji on suffering. As you know, Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji have shared that suffering is not something that happens to us, but rather it's a state of being that we can choose to let go of. In their teachings, Sri Preethaji has said that suffering is often a result of our own self-centric thinking. When we're preoccupied with ourselves, our past, or our future, we become trapped in a cycle of stress and suffering. This is what Sri Preethaji calls "obsessive, self-centric thinking."\n\nImagine, my friend, that you're standing in a river, and the water is flowing rapidly. If you try to swim against the current, you'll exhaust yourself and struggle to make progress. But if you learn to flow with the current, you'll find that you can move effortlessly downstream. Similarly, when we learn to let go of our self-centric thinking and flow with the present moment, we can find peace and freedom from suffering. This is the essence of the Beautiful State, where we're not preoccupied with ourselves, but rather fully present in the moment. As Sri Preethaji has said, "The entire thinking collapses into 'me, me, me.' We are not concerned with finding solutions to the problem at hand." When we're trapped in this cycle of self-centric thinking, we become stuck in our own suffering. But, my friend, there is hope. By recognizing the patterns of our own self-centric thinking and learning to let go of them, we can find freedom from suffering. This is the path to the Beautiful State, where we can live in peace, connection, and joy. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3RyCldrCxL8", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-06 13:16:57+00	{}	default
