ebb32369-4945-4aa8-b4ee-b496a9fc81ab	3a372db1-44a9-441f-a257-65c5e76c0197	Dear seeker, I can see the longing in your heart for a deeper connection with the divine. In our previous conversations, we have touched upon the beautiful state, a consciousness free from suffering. Today, I'd like to offer you a tool to help you navigate your spiritual journey. Let us explore the Three-Question Meditation, a practice that Sri Preethaji shares to return to a beautiful state. This meditation is not about changing your circumstances but about observing yourself in the present moment. It's a gentle reminder to come back to your inner self. As we discussed earlier, the Three-Question Meditation involves observing yourself in three key areas:\n\n1. Are you in a stressful state or a beautiful state? 2. Are you engaged with your past or your future, or are you in the present? 3. Are you preoccupied with yourself, or are you in a state of connection? Take a moment to reflect on these questions. Allow yourself to observe your thoughts, emotions, and physical sensations without judgment. As you inhale and exhale slowly, imagine a gentle flame glowing in the middle of your forehead, bringing a sense of calm and peace. Remember, the goal is not to change your state but to acknowledge and accept it as it is. By doing so, you'll begin to loosen the grip of self-centric thinking and allow the beautiful state to return on its own. As you continue on your spiritual journey, I invite you to return to this meditation whenever you feel the need to reconnect with your inner self. Watch more here:	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pmSPHJfg3AU"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-07 03:36:58+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pmSPHJfg3AU"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 10, "retrieval_queries": ["how can you help me in my journey of spirituality?"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pmSPHJfg3AU", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1mtpheWDhs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCs6I_BNtxo", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1852}	default
15e749b4-361f-453c-a24f-d55598d48d11	029e6593-4018-4325-b958-1f3df17d1707	Dear seeker, I'm glad you asked for a simpler explanation of the Three-Question Meditation. This practice is a beautiful way to return to your beautiful state, and I'm here to guide you through it.\n\nImagine you're sitting in a peaceful space, and you're asking yourself three gentle questions. These questions help you become aware of your current state, which is often clouded by our busy minds.\n\nThe first question is: "Am I in a stressful state or a beautiful state?" This question helps you acknowledge how you're feeling in the moment. Are you feeling anxious, stressed, or overwhelmed, or are you feeling calm, peaceful, and serene? Just observe your state without judgment.\n\nThe second question is: "Am I engaged with my past or my future, or am I in the present?" This question helps you become aware of where your mind is wandering. Are you dwelling on past regrets or future worries, or are you fully present in the moment? When you're in the present, you're free from the burdens of the past and the anxieties of the future.\n\nThe third question is: "Am I preoccupied with myself, or am I in a state of connection?" This question helps you recognize whether you're isolated in your thoughts or connected with the world around you. Are you focused on your own problems, worries, and desires, or are you open to the experiences and perspectives of others?\n\nAs you reflect on these three questions, remember that the goal isn't to change your state or achieve a specific outcome. It's simply to observe yourself with kindness and compassion, allowing your beautiful state to emerge naturally.\n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)"]	0.7075992332895017	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		7.075992332895017	2026-07-07 03:38:26+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier3_complex", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": [], "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 1, "reranked_count": 1, "route_decision": "tier3_complex", "routing_reason": "temporal_query_heuristic", "final_citations": ["Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)"], "retrieved_count": 15, "confidence_score": 7.075992332895017, "needs_web_search": true, "relevant_sources": [], "reranked_sources": [], "retrieval_queries": ["Explain the Three-Question Meditation in simpler terms, which involves observing yourself in three key areas: 1. Are you in a stressful state or a beautiful state? 2. Are you engaged with your past or your future, or are you in the present? 3. Are you preoccupied with yourself, or are you in a state of connection? (also: blissful state, state of bliss, state of calm, state of joy, dhyana)", "Sri Preethaji teachings on Three-Question Meditation", "Three-Question Meditation technique explained simply", "beautiful state vs stressful state meditation"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSNQUkuyB18", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l6svaRx35TI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0u9oe-5HPmk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EqnSkAzfIg", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rGcNJ_Nsuy8", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSAPs1YDkq0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vt_CjAdzebM", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCiK7ABPcrw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWXe9v7PHDs", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zGhlBQ8iWl4"], "final_answer_chars": 16