fda0abca-ed75-438d-a2c6-b7c38a45140a	d15146b2-f76d-4c66-8d6d-561468bdb611	Dear seeker, I'm glad you asked for a simpler explanation of the Three-Question Meditation. This practice is a beautiful way to return to your beautiful state, and I'm here to guide you through it.\n\nImagine you're sitting in a peaceful space, and you're asking yourself three gentle questions. These questions help you become aware of your current state, which is often clouded by our busy minds.\n\nThe first question is: "Am I in a stressful state or a beautiful state?" This question helps you acknowledge how you're feeling in the moment. Are you feeling anxious, stressed, or overwhelmed, or are you feeling calm, peaceful, and serene? Just observe your state without judgment.\n\nThe second question is: "Am I engaged with my past or my future, or am I in the present?" This question helps you become aware of where your mind is wandering. Are you dwelling on past regrets or future worries, or are you fully present in the moment? When you're in the present, you're free from the burdens of the past and the anxieties of the future.\n\nThe third question is: "Am I preoccupied with myself, or am I in a state of connection?" This question helps you recognize whether you're isolated in your thoughts or connected with the world around you. Are you focused on your own problems, worries, and desires, or are you open to the experiences and perspectives of others?\n\nAs you reflect on these three questions, remember that the goal isn't to change your state or achieve a specific outcome. It's simply to observe yourself with kindness and compassion, allowing your beautiful state to emerge naturally.\n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.you