22e4dd04-94f7-4616-9a2f-14a40bc71077	c9dd723a-8f65-4aa9-8731-3526fd4cf714	My dear one, I see that you are seeking to summarize our conversation history and deepen our exploration of the beautiful state, stillness, and consciousness. Let us revisit the key teachings that have guided us thus far. We began by exploring the Serene Mind practice, which Sri Krishnaji offers as a way to cultivate stillness in the midst of chaos. We discussed how this practice can help us return to a calm state of mind, and how it is not just a practice, but a way of being. You then asked about the nature of consciousness and stillness, and how to bridge the gap between active work and silent awareness. We touched on the idea that stillness is not just a state, but a way of being, and that it can be cultivated through practices such as the Serene Mind. We also explored the concept of the three sacred secrets, which Sri Krishnaji teaches as a way to understand the nature of reality and the human experience. These secrets are not just intellectual concepts, but living principles that can guide us in our daily lives. Furthermore, we discussed the difference between a beautiful state and a suffering state, and how our state is constantly sending a signal out to the universe. We saw that our state is shaped by our thoughts, emotions, perceptions, and spiritual energy, and that we have the power to transform our state and live in a beautiful state. In our previous conversation, you asked about maintaining stillness in daily activity, and we explored the Serene Mind practice as a way to cultivate stillness in the midst of chaos. You also asked about the three sacred secrets, and we touched on the idea that these secrets are living principles that can guide us in our daily lives. Now, let us deepen our exploration of these teachings and see how they can guide us in our daily lives. \n\n*(Teachings referenced: Four Sacred Secrets, spiritual vision, inner truth, universal intelligence, spiritual right action, state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["unknown", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319", "Serene Mind — Sri Krishnaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-07 04:51:20+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier3_complex", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWMBvMlGWTA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPHQMD3w9-s"], "low_confidence": true, "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 3, "reranked_count": 3, "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "classifier", "retrieved_count": 16, "relevant_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWMBvMlGWTA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPHQMD3w9-s"], "reranked_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWMBvMlGWTA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPHQMD3w9-s"], "top_rerank_score": 0.0129, "retrieval_queries": ["Based on the conversation history and the latest question, I can determine that the question is a follow-up that refers to previous context.\\n\\nHere's the rewritten question that includes all necessary context from the history:\\n\\n\\"Summarize our conversation so far, which started with exploring how to maintain stillness in daily activity, then delved into the nature of consciousness and stillness, bridging the gap between active work and silent awareness, and discussing Sri Krishnaji's teachings on the three sacred secrets and the difference between a beautiful state and a suffering state.\\"\\n\\nThis rewritten question includes all the necessary context from the conversation history. (also: blissful state, state of bliss, state of calm, state of joy, state of suffering)", "Sri Krishnaji teachings on bridging active wor