9673bc46-1f8b-40f6-926f-0738c9f71359	20db2900-b899-4ace-9d22-feeddaf3c4fd	**Serene Mind Meditation**\n\n1. Settle into a comfortable seat and let your body know it is safe.\n2. Bring attention to conscious breathing: breathe in gently and breathe out slowly.\n3. Notice racing thoughts, overthinking, stress, anger, frustration, grief, or anxiety without fighting them.\n4. Let the breath guide you toward a serene state of calm and inner connection.\n5. When you are ready, gently open your eyes and carry this calm into your next action.	[]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		6.48	2026-07-07 07:58:08+00	{"intent": "MEDITATION", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator"}	default
ce530f61-f75b-436a-81e8-8042893a9ee5	6e764f37-0bdd-40b2-aa39-3ea38898fc5b	Dear one, I sense that you're asking about the external events at Ekam, but let's not forget that the true celebration is within. The Beautiful State is not just a teaching, but a lived experience that can be cultivated in every moment. As we explored earlier, the Beautiful State is a choice we can make, a way of being that is free from stress and filled with connection, joy, and love. It's not bound by time or external events, but rather a state of being that can be accessed in every breath. If you're interested in exploring the Beautiful State further, I'd like to offer you a gentle reminder of the Three-Question Meditation. Take a moment to close your eyes, breathe deeply, and ask yourself: "Am I in a stressful state or a beautiful state?" "Am I engaged with my past or future, or am I present?" "Am I preoccupied with myself or in a state of connection?"\n\nAs you explore these questions, remember that the Beautiful State is not a destination, but a journey. It's a way of living that can be cultivated in every moment, regardless of external events or festivals. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: world centre for enlightenment)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r3iE2gDwIEk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.ekam.org/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-07 07:58:10+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r3iE2gDwIEk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 8, "retrieval_queries": ["When are the upcoming festivals or events at Ekam? (also: ekam world, world centre for enlightenment, world center for enlightenment) varadaiahpalem tirupati andhra pradesh higher consciousness expanded awareness unity consciousness"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r3iE2gDwIEk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vhLVeSDWB5M", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDr00laBiYo"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1731}	default
4dc871d1-3d42-4d87-962e-e8007a5e4e98	735cc035-1092-4a70-8b68-345fdd4d2a14	I hear you, and I want you to know that your feelings are completely valid. In moments like these, the teachings remind us that suffering is a doorway to transformation — not something to fight against, but to move through with awareness.\n\n🧘 **Breathing practice**: Place your hand on your heart. Breathe in slowly — feel your chest rise. Breathe out gently — feel any tension release. Do this 5 times. As Sri Preethaji teaches, 'When you breathe with awareness, you return to the beautiful state.'\n\nWould you like me to guide you through a full Serene Mind meditation? 🙏	[]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		6.48	2026-07-07 07:58:24+00	{"intent": "DISTRESS", "query_tier": "standard", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator"}	default
