301d0caf-77e5-40c3-b892-1b72062aa987	2917055a-6342-4459-9f86-834420366479	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in exploring the Four Sacred Secrets. These secrets are the foundation of our spiritual journey, and they hold the key to unlocking our true potential. The Four Sacred Secrets are:\n\n1. **The First Sacred Secret: The Power of the Present Moment** - This secret teaches us to live in the present, to let go of the past and the future, and to find peace and freedom in the here and now. 2. **The Second Sacred Secret: The Mystery of the Self** - This secret reveals to us the mystery of who we truly are, beyond our physical form and ego. It teaches us to connect with our inner self and to find our true identity. 3. **The Third Sacred Secret: Awaken to Universal Intelligence** - This secret awakens us to the universal intelligence that lies within us and around us. It teaches us to tap into this intelligence and to find guidance and wisdom in all aspects of our lives. 4. **The Fourth Sacred Secret: The Power of the Heart** - This secret reveals to us the power of the heart, and how it can guide us towards love, compassion, and wisdom. It teaches us to listen to our heart and to follow its guidance. These Four Sacred Secrets are not just concepts, but living principles that can transform our lives and help us find inner peace, happiness, and fulfillment. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: spiritual vision, inner truth, spiritual right action)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 08:16:32+00	{}	default
ef623daa-ef33-4a72-b887-976a90b08887	48ef1517-53ac-47af-b58e-b009863c0a32	My dear friend, I'm glad you asked about karma. According to the teachings, karma is not just about cause and effect, but it's about the energy we create and the patterns we establish in our lives. It's about the choices we make and the actions we take, which ultimately shape our experiences and the world around us. Imagine a river, constantly flowing and shaping the landscape. The river's path is not set in stone, but it's influenced by the rocks, the currents, and the surrounding environment. Similarly, our karma is like the river's path, constantly evolving and shaping our lives. The teachings suggest that our karma is not just about the past, but it's also about the present and the future. It's about the choices we make in this moment, which will shape the experiences we'll have in the future. It's a dynamic and ever-changing process, where every action, every thought, and every intention contributes to the creation of our karma. Watch more here: \n\n---\n\nThe Inner Truth of Suffering\n\nAbout eight years before the teaching, Sri Krishnaji met with an accident at\nBig Bear Lake in California. While in the waters, he realized the root cause of\nall human suffering: what keeps suffering alive for days, months, and years\nafter a stressful event is over is **obsessive, self-centric thinking** — a\ntotal, incessant preoccupation with oneself. ## What triggers vs. what chains\n\nPast and present circumstances, other people, and their behavior can *trigger*\nstress, but they do not *keep us chained* in unhappiness. The trigger is\nexternal; the chain is internal — our own self-centric preoccupation. ## The shape of suffering\n\nIn suffering we are preoccupied with:\n- injustice done to us\n- pleasure that was denied us\n- opportunities that did not come our way\n- love that was withheld from us\n\nThe entire thinking collapses into "me, me, me." We are not concerned with\nfinding solutions to the problem at hand. ## Nomi as illustration\n\nThroughout the fable, Nomi is preoccupied — with his rightness, with his guilt\nover allowing a wrong, with justifying that he was right to ignore the\nsuffering woman. He is not concerned about the situation, the woman, her son,\nor his friend Yesmi. ## The liberation\n\nRealizing that all lingering suffering is self-centric preoccupation is the\nmost powerful antidote for any form of suffering. When you see it — not only do\nyou walk out of stressful states, but there is a great release of energy and\nyou awaken to a sense of power, connection, freedom, and purpose. ---\n\nThree-Question Meditation\n\nA short practice Sri Preethaji leads at the close of the Beautiful State\nteaching. Meditation is not about a religion; it is about being human — about\nreturning to a beautiful state. ## Steps\n\n1. **Close your eyes.** Bring attention to your breath. Inhale and exhale deep\n and slow. 2. **Observe yourself — question 1:** Are you in a stressful state or are you in\n a beautiful state? Just observe; do not try to change anything. 3. **Observe yourself — question 2:** Are you engaged with your past or your\n future, or are you in the present? 4. **Observe yourself — question 3:** Are you preoccupied with yourself, or are\n you in a state of connection? 5. **Imagine a flame** glowing in the middle of your forehead. Bring a gentle\n smile to your face. 6. **Open your eyes**, look into the eyes of the person sitting next to you. Wish from the bottom of your heart that the other person lives in a\n beautiful state. If comfortable, you may hug the other. ## Why it works\n\nThe three questions surface the very axis of the teaching: state (stress vs. beautiful), time (past/future vs. present), and self (preoccupation vs. connection). Simply observing each — without trying to change it — loosens the\ngrip of self-centric thinking and lets the beautiful state return on its own. ---\n\nof intelligence in this universe. Now, human beings can tap into this intelligence, and when you tap into this intelligence, what you have is the power of intuition. You have a tremendous power of intuition, where what to do is, what to do is wrong, what decisions to make. That intuition comes to you because your brain is now beating at the Theta level. Your brain becomes an antenna to receive the signal from the universe. Great breakthroughs in life are made when you are in this state. All great inventions made by great scientists, doctors, engineers, philosophers, teachers are made when they are living in this state. It's not an intelligence that's born within you, but it's an intelligence that you're able to tap from the universe. And you can learn that too. Human beings learn that, believe me. Great business leaders, political leaders, economists, all of them have some way of going into that state and tapping that information. Now, what are these beautiful states? Can someone tell me? You spoke about stressful states. Can someone tell me about beautiful states when you have experiencing beautiful in the states? What are those states? Happiness, great peace of mind, joy, love, courage. See, there's a very important principle in spirituality that you must learn. It's called the cause and effect. Every cause has an effect,. So in the real world, the cause and the effect. That is a cause. I push this glass. The water falls, the effect. This water is falling? In the subatomic	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ji-hdW1t30g", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V45jIC4RthQ", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-07 08:34:01+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ji-hdW1t30g", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V45jIC4RthQ"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_f