664c72ba-2195-4673-b71b-90535c8b5500	25311143-e7ca-4555-ae27-4dafc4d70b97	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in exploring the Four Sacred Secrets. These secrets are the foundation of our spiritual journey, and they hold the key to unlocking our true potential. The Four Sacred Secrets are:\n\n1. **The First Sacred Secret: The Power of the Present Moment** - This secret teaches us to live in the present, to let go of the past and the future, and to find peace and freedom in the here and now. 2. **The Second Sacred Secret: The Mystery of the Self** - This secret reveals to us the mystery of who we truly are, beyond our physical form and ego. It teaches us to connect with our inner self and to find our true identity. 3. **The Third Sacred Secret: Awaken to Universal Intelligence** - This secret awakens us to the universal intelligence that lies within us and around us. It teaches us to tap into this intelligence and to find guidance and wisdom in all aspects of our lives. 4. **The Fourth Sacred Secret: The Power of the Heart** - This secret reveals to us the power of the heart, and how it can guide us towards love, compassion, and wisdom. It teaches us to listen to our heart and to follow its guidance. These Four Sacred Secrets are not just concepts, but living principles that can transform our lives and help us find inner peace, happiness, and fulfillment. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: spiritual vision, inner truth, spiritual right action)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 16:31:50+00	{}	default
4fd246c8-6223-4478-9d43-7e677ad2f9f8	e1c5a6eb-3425-4171-903f-bf6fc878b90b	Dear seeker, as you delve into the beautiful state, I'd like to share that both Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji emphasize its importance in achieving a state of inner peace and harmony. According to Sri Preethaji, "The beautiful state is the foundation of a serene mind". In this state, one is able to let go of all that's not needed, allowing for true freedom and clarity. Sri Krishnaji also resonates with the idea of the beautiful state, suggesting that it's a space where we can transcend our conditioning and connect with our true nature. He says, "The beautiful state is not something that you can achieve, it's a recognition of what already is". This recognition allows us to see the world with fresh eyes and experience life with greater joy and wonder. As you explore the beautiful state, remember that it's not just a mental concept, but a lived experience that can bring depth and meaning to your life. *(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "unknown", "https://www.breathingroom.com/", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown"]	0.713039215250708	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		6.81	2026-07-07 16:31:51+00	{"intent": "RELATIONAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": null, "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "model_provider": "nim", "relevant_count": 3, "reranked_count": 4, "route_decision": "deep", "routing_reason": "classifier", "final_citations": ["Beautiful State — Sri Preethaji (YouTube https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqxxCYnAxo8)", "unknown", "https://www.breathingroom.com/", "unknown", "unknown", "unknown"], "retrieved_count": 20, "confidence_score": 6.81, "relevant_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4"], "reranked_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wDaE92bNRNw"], "retrieval_queries": ["Compare Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji on the beautiful state. (also: blissful state, state of bliss, state of calm, state of joy, preetha ji)", "Sri Preethaji teachings beautiful state", "Sri Krishnaji teachings on the beautiful state", "Krishnaji Preethaji teachings comparison beautiful state"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vARTudIEq30", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wDaE92bNRNw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZXuNv0L8YA", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-mTRlE0TC4", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sCiK7ABPcrw", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AR0r8B6Ga8E", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=88NOQTz5_yI"], "final_answer_chars": 998, "llm_expansion_count": 3, "verification_passed": true, "generated_answer_chars": 1507, "grading_skipped_high_confidence": true}	default
17bceb7d-7c6c-449c-a999-ccee476a2b16	6d9a9074-54bf-498e-8569-737e11bb6b13	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in exploring the long exhale breathing. This practice is an essential part of cultivating a Serene Mind, as taught by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. To practice the long exhale breathing, start by finding a comfortable seated position with your back straight. Close your eyes and take a deep breath in through your nose, filling your lungs completely. Now, slowly exhale through your mouth, allowing your breath to become long and smooth. Imagine that you're exhaling all the tension and stress out of your body. As you exhale, feel your body relax and let go of any resistance. Continue to breathe in this way, focusing on the sensation of the breath moving in and out of your body. Remember, the key is to make the exhale longer than the inhale, allowing your body to release and relax.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		8.0	2026-07-07 16:31:57+00	{"intent": "FACTUAL", "model_used": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "query_tier": "tier2_simple", "memory_used": true, "citation_urls": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c"], "model_provider": "nim", "route_decision": "tier2_simple", "routing_reason": "pre_classified_from_pipeline_coordinator", "retrieved_count": 9, "retrieval_queries": ["How do I practice the long exhale breathing?"], "retrieved_sources": ["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgQV_5FjPNk", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tl2Ek-QakME", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2z5qxSr4EaI"], "llm_expansion_count": 0, "generated_answer_chars": 1530}	default
317fdeba-b29c-4322-aa41-d887a65f10be	99eaf350-9ec8-43bb-bd38-1ca63c4d3d4d	Dear one, a beautiful state is a profound concept that Sri Preethaji teaches us about. It's a state of consciousness where we live free from suffering. In this state, we experience connection, joy, love, compassion, vitality, and passion. It's a state where we are not bound by stress, anxiety, or any other form of suffering. Imagine living a life where every moment is filled with love, compassion, and connection. Where every interaction is a beautiful dance of give and take, where we are not just thinking about ourselves, but also about the other person. This is the beautiful state. As Sri Preethaji says, "If you are not in a beautiful state, your default state is stress." So, it's essential to understand that the beautiful state is not just a feeling or an emotion; it's a choice we can make every moment of our lives. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oZRQoiRe7s4"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 16:32:01+00	{}	default
