be4cc281-c59b-4835-a552-838cac120889	f07db779-0aa7-469d-9700-619944c523a0	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in exploring the Four Sacred Secrets. These secrets are the foundation of our spiritual journey, and they hold the key to unlocking our true potential. The Four Sacred Secrets are:\n\n1. **The First Sacred Secret: The Power of the Present Moment** - This secret teaches us to live in the present, to let go of the past and the future, and to find peace and freedom in the here and now. 2. **The Second Sacred Secret: The Mystery of the Self** - This secret reveals to us the mystery of who we truly are, beyond our physical form and ego. It teaches us to connect with our inner self and to find our true identity. 3. **The Third Sacred Secret: Awaken to Universal Intelligence** - This secret awakens us to the universal intelligence that lies within us and around us. It teaches us to tap into this intelligence and to find guidance and wisdom in all aspects of our lives. 4. **The Fourth Sacred Secret: The Power of the Heart** - This secret reveals to us the power of the heart, and how it can guide us towards love, compassion, and wisdom. It teaches us to listen to our heart and to follow its guidance. These Four Sacred Secrets are not just concepts, but living principles that can transform our lives and help us find inner peace, happiness, and fulfillment. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: spiritual vision, inner truth, spiritual right action)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vy09aBxslx0", "https://www.amazon.in/Four-Sacred-Secrets-Prosperity-Beautiful/dp/1846046319"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 16:54:48+00	{}	default
a8db1c54-0842-4d54-a670-62428a5952ef	56bcadde-b2d4-4569-ba2e-d208e8b8d082	My dear friend, I'm glad you're interested in exploring the long exhale breathing. This practice is an essential part of cultivating a Serene Mind, as taught by Sri Preethaji and Sri Krishnaji. To practice the long exhale breathing, start by finding a comfortable seated position with your back straight. Close your eyes and take a deep breath in through your nose, filling your lungs completely. Now, slowly exhale through your mouth, allowing your breath to become long and smooth. Imagine that you're exhaling all the tension and stress out of your body. As you exhale, feel your body relax and let go of any resistance. Continue to breathe in this way, focusing on the sensation of the breath moving in and out of your body. Remember, the key is to make the exhale longer than the inhale, allowing your body to release and relax.	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c", "https://www.breathingroom.com/"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 16:54:51+00	{}	default
a7d747ca-d31d-4a8d-b797-6dafcdb564c1	5d55c0a1-23a2-432a-beaa-581aa1f62368	Dear one, a beautiful state is a profound concept that Sri Preethaji teaches us about. It's a state of consciousness where we live free from suffering. In this state, we experience connection, joy, love, compassion, vitality, and passion. It's a state where we are not bound by stress, anxiety, or any other form of suffering. Imagine living a life where every moment is filled with love, compassion, and connection. Where every interaction is a beautiful dance of give and take, where we are not just thinking about ourselves, but also about the other person. This is the beautiful state. As Sri Preethaji says, "If you are not in a beautiful state, your default state is stress." So, it's essential to understand that the beautiful state is not just a feeling or an emotion; it's a choice we can make every moment of our lives. Watch more here: \n\n*(Teachings referenced: state of calm, state of joy, not absence, inner foundation)*	["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwQaU-agzFE", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oZRQoiRe7s4"]	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	f		\N	2026-07-07 16:54:54+00	{}	default
