0b351436-e987-5f8a-9006-c243ddc1aa53	841b700a-da9a-4d52-9e0c-68a799735e00	1783358847.3164163	"[{\\"role\\": \\"user\\", \\"content\\": \\"Share a teaching from Sri Preethaji on suffering\\"}, {\\"role\\": \\"assistant\\", \\"content\\": \\"My dear friend, I'm so glad you're interested in exploring the teachings of Sri Preethaji on suffering. As we've discussed earlier, the root cause of all human suffering is often found in our own obsessive, self-centric thinking. This thinking can keep us chained in unhappiness, even after the initial trigger has passed. Sri Preethaji beautifully illustrates this concept through the story of Nomi, who is preoccupied with his own rightness, guilt, and justifications, rather than finding solutions to the problem at hand. This self-centric thinking is a common pattern that can lead us away from the present moment and into a state of suffering. In this sense, suffering is not something that happens to us, but rather it's a reflection of our own thinking patterns. By becoming aware of these patterns and letting go of our attachment to them, we can begin to break free from the chains of suffering and move towards a more peaceful and connected state. As Sri Preethaji so eloquently puts it, \\\\\\"Realizing that all lingering suffering is self-centric preoccupation is the most powerful antidote for any form of suffering.\\\\\\" This realization can be a powerful catalyst for change, allowing us to awaken to a sense of power, connection, freedom, and purpose. Watch more here:\\"}]"	{https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3RyCldrCxL8,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAMJEgwaPEc}	"[{\\"timestamp\\": 1783358847.316417, \\"distress_level\\": 0, \\"provoked\\": false, \\"topic\\": \\"QUERY\\"}]"	{}
