50e86e38-5b81-5284-a097-6261aa41709d	9f55981a-9ba3-4dca-afda-d4a8d9763f34	1783398856.1697245	"[{\\"role\\": \\"user\\", \\"content\\": \\"How do I maintain stillness in daily activity?\\"}, {\\"role\\": \\"assistant\\", \\"content\\": \\"My dear one, you seek to embody stillness in the midst of daily activity. This is a beautiful aspiration, for it is in stillness that we find our true nature. Sri Krishnaji's Serene Mind practice can guide us in this endeavor. Remember, the Serene Mind is not just a practice, but a way of being. It's a state of consciousness that can be cultivated in the midst of chaos. To maintain stillness in daily activity, begin by acknowledging that stillness is not about physical inactivity, but about being present in the midst of activity. As you go about your day, bring your attention to your breath. Feel the sensation of the air moving in and out of your body. As you inhale, imagine fresh energy entering your being, and as you exhale, imagine any tension or stress leaving your body. When you find yourself getting caught up in thoughts or emotions, gently bring your attention back to your breath. Remember, the goal is not to suppress your emotions or thoughts, but to observe them with kindness and curiosity. In the Serene Mind practice, we are encouraged to recognize the emotion arising within us, and then observe the direction of our thinking. Are we entangled in the past or the future, or are we present in the moment? By acknowledging and observing our thoughts and emotions, we can begin to let go of our attachment to them, and find stillness in the midst of activity. Watch more here:\\"}]"	{https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EqnSkAzfIg,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fKvjHOD_kQ,https://www.breathingroom.com/}	"[{\\"timestamp\\": 1783398856.1697276, \\"distress_level\\": 0, \\"provoked\\": false, \\"topic\\": \\"QUERY\\"}]"	{}
